# codebase-memory-mcp: keep the Board 4 kit and the generated spec tables out of the product's graph.
# The kit's ui/ files are copies of portal/ui, so every portal symbol would answer twice (a duplicate-definition query becomes noise), and C*.md, states.md and portal-diff.md are generated tables with thousands of headings.
# The kit has its own graph: index_repository --repo_path docs/pins2/kit.
docs/pins2/kit/
docs/pins2/final/board4-spec/C*.md
docs/pins2/final/board4-spec/states.md
docs/pins2/final/board4-spec/portal-diff.md
# codebase-memory-mcp index scope (read at the repo root on every index and auto-sync).
# .claude/ is on the tool's built-in skip list, but here it holds tracked code: 78 hook scripts and their tests, 22 rule files and settings.json. Un-skip it so callers and definitions in hooks are answerable.
!.claude/
# Session worktrees under .claude/ are full copies of the repo; indexing them would duplicate every symbol.
.claude/worktrees/
# Minified vendor bundles: no human-written symbols, and they crowd semantic search results.
*.min.js
